**Status:** Merged to `main` and main-inspected for the declared metadata-only event-log backend contract scope; assistant sandbox syntax/helper/mock-smoke checks, package extraction/recheck, artifact guard, Michael local Windows/MINGW64 deterministic checks, Michael local Windows/MINGW64 real-runtime confidence checks, direct GitHub branch inspection, and direct GitHub `main` inspection passed.

---

## 1. Purpose

This branch defines a narrow, modular, metadata-only backend contract surface for future durable action-event / audit storage backends.

It answers the contract questions left open by `runtime-event-log-store-runtime-wiring-v1` without implementing storage:

```text
future eventLogStoreBackend identity
backend definition metadata shape
backend status vocabulary
best-effort / buffered / fail-closed append policy vocabulary
runtime wait-mode vocabulary as metadata only
append error-surface vocabulary as metadata only
read capability metadata for durable / cursor / bounded-history fallback distinction
linkage to the existing action-event log store contract
```

This branch intentionally does **not** make action events durable. It does not pick SQLite, PostgreSQL, file storage, a DB connection shape, adapter factory behavior, runtime backend injection, or public durable read APIs.

