## 11. Caveats / known risks

### Finding: Backend contract is metadata-only

Affected surface:

```text
eventLogStoreBackend, database/file persistence, restart recovery
```

Why it matters:

```text
This branch names the backend kind and policy vocabulary but does not make action events durable.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Use a later integration/adapter branch to define backend selection and concrete storage behavior.
```

### Finding: fail-closed is vocabulary only

Affected surface:

```text
audit strictness, append failure behavior, execute-action settlement
```

Why it matters:

```text
The current runtime remains no-adapter/best-effort/non-durable.
This branch does not make append failures fatal.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
A later runtime integration branch must explicitly wire fail-closed semantics and tests before claiming strict audit behavior.
```

### Finding: buffered is vocabulary only

Affected surface:

```text
append queueing, backpressure, retry/drain behavior
```

Why it matters:

```text
No buffer queue, drain behavior, retry policy, or shutdown interaction was implemented.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Keep buffered policy as metadata until a separate buffer design branch exists.
```

### Finding: real-runtime tests were confidence checks, not required by declared scope

Affected surface:

```text
verification language / merge-readiness notes
```

Why it matters:

```text
This branch did not touch runtime wiring, worker/native execution, lifecycle, request settlement, or stream behavior.
The real-runtime checks are useful confidence but should not imply the branch changed native/model behavior.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Record real-runtime checks as Michael-run confidence checks, not as evidence of new runtime backend behavior.
```

### Finding: final dev-notes.61 status needed refresh after merge

Affected surface:

```text
docs/source-truth hygiene
```

Why it matters:

```text
At final checkout time, GitHub main docs/dev-notes.61 still showed candidate-staged wording and did not record merge/main-inspection or Michael's real-runtime confidence checks.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Replace or refresh docs/dev-notes.61 with this final document.
```

### Finding: docs/dev-notes.60 stale duplicate was not repaired

Affected surface:

```text
docs/source-truth hygiene
```

Why it matters:

```text
Preflight found docs/dev-notes.60 and docs/dev-note.60 had different final-status wording in the uploaded mirror / GitHub context.
This branch intentionally did not mix that status cleanup into the contract branch.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Handle dev-notes.60 cleanup as a separate docs-aside if Michael approves.
```

